{"repositoryId":1420053736,"availability":"available","full":"CyrusNamjoo/ab-testing-toolkit","name":"ab-testing-toolkit","description":"A/B testing toolkit with trust checks (SRM), frequentist + Bayesian inference, power analysis, multiple-testing-corrected segments, uplift modelling and a Streamlit dashboard.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-15T02:02:36Z","updated":"2026-10-15T02:46:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cyrus-ab-testing.streamlit.app/","topics":["ab-testing","bayesian-statistics","causal-inference","data-analytics","experimentation","python","statistics","streamlit","uplift-modeling"],"demo":"https://cyrus-ab-testing.streamlit.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:45.109Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:45.109Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:45.109Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T02:59:45.109Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Live demo: cyrus-ab-testing.streamlit.app (may take 30 seconds to wake up)","abkit is a Python toolkit that takes raw A/B test sessions and returns a decision you can defend: ship, hold, extend or reject. Before it reports an uplift, it checks whether the experiment itself can be trusted. Then it reads the result in both frequentist and Bayesian terms, tests guardrails, checks whether the test was big enough, corrects segment analysis for multiple testing, and fits an uplift model to see whether personalisation is worth it.","I ran it on four website experiments (online education, travel booking, charity donations, SaaS free trial). Variation B \"won\" all four on the headline numbers. The pipeline recommends shipping three of them, holds the fourth because its traffic split is off, and flags caveats a dashboard would hide."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CyrusNamjoo/ab-testing-toolkit/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e0